## The Expanse: Osiris Reborn at a glance

The Expanse: Osiris Reborn is a story-driven, third-person action RPG set in the universe of The Expanse novels and TV series. It is developed and published by Owlcat Games, the studio behind the Pathfinder RPGs and Warhammer 40,000: Rogue Trader. The Steam listing gives a release window of **Q2 2027**, with no calendar day yet, checked 27 November 2026.

## What we know so far

- **Developer and publisher:** Owlcat Games.
- **Release window:** Q2 2027 on Steam, meaning April to June 2027. No exact date has been announced.
- **Platforms:** the official site links to Steam, PlayStation 5 and Xbox versions.
- **Price:** not listed on Steam yet.
- **Languages:** full audio in English, with text in French, German, Spanish, Russian, Simplified Chinese and Brazilian Portuguese, according to Steam.
- **Trailers:** Owlcat's YouTube channel has a Gameplay Reveal Trailer, a Gameplay Trailer and a "Becoming a captain" video.

## The story

You are no hero. Owlcat casts you as a mercenary with Pinkwater Security whose short shore leave on the asteroid Eros goes badly wrong. You're trapped in a deadly lockdown and pulled into a conspiracy that spans the solar system. To survive, you take command of what the store page calls the most advanced ship in the solar system, while dealing with political pressure and an enemy that wants you dead.

## Your captain and crew

You create your own captain and choose an origin: **Earther, Martian or Belter**, the three factions of The Expanse. You lead a crew of specialists, and Owlcat says your relationships with them grow or break down depending on your choices and how you lead. The ship is presented as your home, where trust has to be earned.

## Combat

Fights are third-person, with cover-based gunplay and abilities. Two companions join you in the field, while other crew members support from a distance, for example by disabling systems or drawing enemy attention. You give real-time commands to your squad.

## Where you'll go

The Steam description names well-known locations from The Expanse, including **Ganymede, Ceres, Mars and Luna**. You can explore ruined habitats and political strongholds, talk to locals and use your skills to change what happens next.

## PC requirements

Steam lists only Windows 10 so far. The processor, graphics card and storage requirements haven't been published.

## What's still unconfirmed

- **Release day:** only the Q2 2027 window is on Steam.
- **Price and editions:** not announced on Steam yet.
- **PC requirements:** beyond Windows 10, none are listed.
- **Performance:** we haven't played The Expanse: Osiris Reborn.

